  "rationale": "**Structural obligations.** The requirement `requirements.sdk.graph.context-tools.outline_source.fn` has two structural parts:\n1. `SourceAnalysis<P: SourceProvider>` offers `pub async fn parse(&self, id: &ResourceId) -> Result<ParsedSource, P::Error>`.\n2. The SDK exposes an `outline_source` command through its source tools.\n\n**Obligation 1: the `parse` method.**\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/src/sources.rs#impl[SourceAnalysis<P>]/fn[parse]` has exactly the required signature.\n- It sits in `impl<P: SourceProvider> SourceAnalysis<P>`, which matches the bound in the requirement.\n- It is async, takes `&self` and `&ResourceId`, and returns `Result<ParsedSource, P::Error>`.\n- It delegates to `self.provider.parse(id, &self.languages)`.\n\n**Obligation 2: exposing the command.**\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/sources.rs#impl[SourceSession<'_, P, F, D::NodeId, D::EdgeLabel>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[definitions]` declares a tool named `outline_source`. Its schema requires a `resource` with `scheme` and `location`.\n- The same file's `fn[dispatch]` handles `\"outline_source\"`. It calls `analysis.parse(&resource)` and returns the resource and the outline nodes' selectors and kinds.\n- Reaching `dispatch` and the `parse` call needed no extra implementation marker. `dispatch` is a separate item carrying the `outline_source.behavior` and `outline_source.inputs` markers, so I did not assess it against those refining declarations.\n\n**Gaps.** I found no structural gap. There are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments. This was a structural assessment only, so I did not assess runtime behavior or test evidence.",
